    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4e54fbdfdf8dd0b9f0b36d227e331aaaacee9dd21a7b8a49623f8a31ec8a6d78",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source builds a two-scale transfer from off-axis control of H_t to zero density. Saddle analysis makes the first Fourier mode dominant on a logarithmically lowered line and holomorphy supplies logarithmic-derivative control; the resulting argument-principle estimates give the global count, while a rescaled normal-family argument forces a linear logarithmic profile and thereby recovers the mesoscopic count.",
