    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b996f6767b08bce7037ff3118f80cfead600f8bc77bfd9cb0ddd236b04f7a55b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Deliberately weak small-gap control functions as analytic infrastructure rather than as an equilibrium conclusion. Cluster virial and exterior-energy estimates propagate an extreme gap defect until mesoscopic spacing blocks it; the resulting subpolynomial reciprocal-gap bound seeds a spatial-pigeonhole argument that obtains polynomial time-integrated energy, and those two controls together dominate the infinite sums needed to differentiate the localized Hamiltonian.",
